sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Microservice App
    participant GW as Gateway Ingress (Virtual Key Auth)
    participant Guard as Pre/Post Guardrail
    participant Cache as Redis (Exact & Semantic Cache)
    participant Router as Model Router & LB
    participant Primary as Primary LLM (e.g. Claude 3.5 Sonnet)
    participant Fallback as Fallback LLM (e.g. GPT-4o)
    participant Telemetry as Telemetry & Spend Audit

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/chat/completions (Bearer sk-team-virtual-key)
    Note over GW: 1. Validate key authenticity<br/>2. Enforce monthly budget & RPM/TPM limits

    alt Budget Exceeded
        GW-->>Client: 400 Bad Request (BudgetExceededError)
    else Budget Valid
        GW->>Guard: Inspect payload for prompt injection & PII
        Note over Guard: Scrub sensitive tokens: [REDACTED_EMAIL]
        Guard->>Cache: Query SHA-256 hash & Vector Embedding

        alt Cache Hit (Exact or Semantic Similarity >= 0.85)
            Cache-->>GW: Return Cached Response (0ms LLM Latency, $0.00 Cost)
            GW->>Telemetry: Emit Cache-Hit Span (OTel)
            GW-->>Client: 200 OK (Instant Cached Completion)
        else Cache Miss
            Cache-->>Router: Cache Miss: Proceed to dispatch
            Router->>Primary: POST /v1/chat/completions (Primary Deployment)

            alt Primary Provider Fails (HTTP 429 Rate Limit or 503 Outage)
                Primary-->>Router: HTTP 429 Too Many Requests
                Note over Router: Activate Fallback Cascade & trigger cooldown
                Router->>Fallback: POST /v1/chat/completions (Backup Provider)
                Fallback-->>Router: 200 OK (Response Generated)
                Router->>Cache: Asynchronously store response in Redis
                Router->>Guard: Evaluate output moderation & JSON schema
                Guard->>Telemetry: Record token spend, latency, and fallback attribution
                Telemetry-->>GW: Metric recorded against virtual key
                GW-->>Client: 200 OK (Response with x-litellm-model: gpt-4o)
            else Primary Provider Succeeds
                Primary-->>Router: 200 OK (Response Generated)
                Router->>Cache: Store response with 24h TTL
                Router->>Guard: Evaluate output moderation & JSON schema
                Guard->>Telemetry: Record token spend against virtual key
                Telemetry-->>GW: Spend updated in PostgreSQL
                GW-->>Client: 200 OK (Response with x-litellm-model: claude-3-5-sonnet)
            end
        end
    end
